Great question! Here's the exact workflow every time you start ngrok:

## Every Time You Start ngrok (Free Tier):

### Step 1: Start Django (if not running)

```bash
cd backend
python manage.py runserver 8000
```

### Step 2: Start ngrok

```bash
ngrok http 8000
```

### Step 3: Copy the NEW ngrok URL

You'll see something like:

```javascript
Forwarding  https://sharpie-carless-rimless.ngrok-free.dev -> http://localhost:8000
```

__Copy the HTTPS URL__ (the one starting with `https://`)

### Step 4: Update Webhook URL in MeSomb Dashboard

1. Login to [](https://dashboard.mesomb.com)<https://dashboard.mesomb.com>

2. Go to __Settings → Webhooks__

3. __Delete the old webhook URL__ (if it exists)

4. __Add new webhook URL__:

   ```javascript
   https://sharpie-carless-rimless.ngrok-free.dev/api/payments/webhooks/mesomb/
   ```

   (Replace with your actual ngrok URL from Step 3)

5. Save the webhook configuration

### Step 5: Test the Webhook

Make a test payment and watch Django logs for `[WEBHOOK]` messages

## Important Notes:

⚠️ __Free ngrok URLs change every time__ you restart ngrok ⚠️ __You MUST update the webhook URL__ in MeSomb dashboard each time ⚠️ __Keep ngrok running__ while testing payments

## Quick Checklist:

✅ Django running on port 8000 ✅ ngrok running with `ngrok http 8000` ✅ Copied the new ngrok HTTPS URL ✅ Updated webhook URL in MeSomb dashboard ✅ Tested with a payment

## For Production (When Deployed):

Once you deploy to production with a real domain (e.g., `https://yourdomain.com`), the webhook URL will be permanent and you won't need to update it:

```javascript
https://yourdomain.com/api/payments/webhooks/mesomb/
```

__Summary: Start ngrok → Copy new URL → Update in MeSomb dashboard → Test payment__
